Package: SegStability
Type: Package
Title: Descriptive Segmentation Sensitivity in Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Rama Krishna", "Pudota",
    email = "ramakrishnapudota36@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides infrastructure for descriptive segmentation-sensitivity
    analysis in molecule-resolved spatial transcriptomics. The intended analyses
    compare alternative segmentations of the same immutable molecule universe
    and describe effects on categorical cell-state conclusions. This initial
    development version provides lossless universe identity and certified
    segmentation partitions and shared-universe segmentation sets, complete
    pairwise shared-molecule correspondence, directional dominance and
    structural component summaries, and explicit validation reports for
    scientific consistency, optional spatial inputs, integrity and provenance
    completeness, and categorical state stability with explicit unresolved
    evidence and full-population accounting, and directional support sensitivity
    preserving original graph semantics and denominators, and optional spatial
    reciprocal-anchor topology with explicit geometry eligibility and observation
    windows, and direct polygon-overlap comparison with derived maximum-IoU
    matching preserving the primary molecule correspondence, and label-invariant
    stochastic replicate agreement with full-universe assignment-status
    accounting and conditional partition agreement, and conservative optional
    molecule-container ingestion and geometry interoperability with explicit
    scientific identity and census evidence. Results do not rank segmentation
    accuracy.
